{"step_index":611,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:02:28Z","content":"I will create the comprehensive canonical audit implementation plan in `implementation_plan.md`.","thinking":"**Begin Audit Planning**\n\nI've fixed all the date-related JavaScript errors! The dashboard should be error-free regarding dates. I'm now starting to draft the comprehensive audit implementation plan.\n\n\n**Defining Audit Scope**\n\nI've defined the audit's scope: a plan to check the digest generator against the 2010 Lviv and Dolnytsky Typikons, identifying rubrical errors and inconsistencies. I've established the audit's canonical grounding, referencing *Ordo Celebrationis*, Dolnytsky, and the 2010 Lviv Typikon. I'm focusing on the twenty canonical paradigms for the audit's dimensions.\n\n\n**Detailing Audit Metrics**\n\nI've established the second audit dimension: office-by-office rubrics and choreography. For Vespers, I'm noting Kathisma determination, stichera count ratios, Dogmatikon selection rules, and triggers for Litiya and Artoklasia. Matins focuses on \"God is the Lord\" vs. \"Alleluia,\" Kathismata rotation, the Polyeleos, and Canon odes, along with the Doxology. I'm checking Hours' cycling and Liturgy's Antiphon selection and entrance sequences.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":true,\"Summary\":\"Comprehensive Canonical Typikon Source Audit Implementation Plan.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"<!-- [GENERATOR: Gemini 3.7 Flash] -->\\n# Implementation Plan — Comprehensive Canonical Typikon Source Audit\\n\\nThis implementation plan establishes the methodology, benchmark test suite, and correction pipeline to canonically audit the Typikon Coded digest generator and engine resolvers against the **2010 Lviv Typikon** and the **Dolnytsky Typikon Parts II–V**.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Objective & Canonical Authority Hierarchy\\n\\nThe objective is to eliminate all rubrical hallucinations, erroneous hymn distribution ratios, and structural discrepancies in the generated Service Rubrics Digest, ensuring 100% fidelity to canonical Ruthenian/UGCC liturgical usage.\\n\\n### Hierarchy of Authority (Rule 2):\\n1. **Ordo Celebrationis** (Rome, 1944 / 1996) — Primary rubrical standard for service choreography.\\n2. **Dolnytsky Typikon Parts II–V** (Lviv, 1899) — Detailed rubrics for the daily cycle, Menaion, Triodion, and Pentecostarion.\\n3. **2010 Lviv Typikon** — The authoritative modern UGCC codification.\\n4. **Liturgicon & Horologion** — Verbatim prayers, litanies, and ordos.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Scope of the Canonical Audit\\n\\nThe audit covers all six core liturgical dimensions across the 20 Canonical Paradigms:\\n\\n```\\n┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\\n│                    Canonical Audit Dimensions & Checkpoints                  │\\n├──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\\n│ 1. Vespers Architecture                                                      │\\n│    • Kathisma assignment (Saturday evening Kathisma 1; Weekday Kathisma cycle)│\\n│    • Stichera at \\\"Lord, I Call\\\" (Total count 10, 8, 6, 4; exac\n<truncated 7543 bytes>","Description":"\"Create Comprehensive Canonical Typikon Source Audit Implementation Plan\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\augus\\\\/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/implementation_plan.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing implementation plan for canonical audit\"","toolSummary":"\"Writing implementation_plan.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
