ines [Y-Z]\r\n28: \r\n29: #### Step 1: Locate Orders\r\n30: - [ ] Find \"ORDER OF [SERVICE]\" header\r\n31: - [ ] Note exact line numbers\r\n32: \r\n33: #### Step 2: Extract Elements (Variant 1: [TYPE])\r\n34: | # | Element | Typikon Line\n<truncated 748 bytes>\nitations to rubrics\r\n55: - [ ] Validate JSON\r\n56: \r\n57: #### Step 7: Create Stress Tests\r\n58: - [ ] 2-saint scenario\r\n59: - [ ] Feast + saint collision\r\n60: - [ ] Seasonal override (Lent, Pascha)\r\n61: ```\r\n62: \r\n63: ---\r\n64: \r\n65: ## Quick Reference: Key Typikon Sections\r\n66: \r\n67: | Section | Content | Audit Priority |\r\n68: |:--------|:--------|:---------------|\r\n69: | Part I: Orders | Service structures | HIGH |\r\n70: | Part II: Paradigms | 20 stacking rules | HIGH |\r\n71: | Part III: Menaion | Fixed feast rubrics | MEDIUM |\r\n72: | Part IV: Triodion | Lenten/Paschal overrides | HIGH |\r\n73: | Part V: Temple | Temple feast rules | LOW |\r\n74: | Footnotes | Exception clarifications | AS NEEDED |\r\n75: \r\n76: ---\r\n77: \r\n78: ## Maximum Liturgical Day (Stress Test Baseline)\r\n79: \r\n80: Per Dolnytsky Part II Line 31:\r\n81: > **\"The ecclesiastical rubric does NOT provide for more than TWO services to saints [on one day].\"**\r\n82: \r\n83: | Scenario | Components | Complexity |\r\n84: |:---------|:-----------|:-----------|\r\n85: | Sunday + 2 Saints | Resurrection + 2 Menaion | MAX |\r\n86: | Great Feast + Saint | Feast dominates | HIGH |\r\n87: | Forefeast + 2 Saints | e.g., November 2 | HIGH |\r\n88: | Lenten Weekday + Saint | Triodion + Menaion | MEDIUM |\r\n89: | Afterfeast + Apodosis + 2 Saints | Ultimate edge case | EXTREME |\r\n90: \r\n91: ---\r\n92: \r\n93: ## Replication Instructions for Other Models\r\n94: \r\n95: 1. **Start with typikon_search_methodology.md** — Follow 7 steps exactly\r\n96: 2. **Use this template** — Copy audit checklist for each service\r\n97: 3. **Reference matins_variants_gap_matrix.md** — Pattern for element comparison\r\n98: 4. **App