{"step_index":637,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T23:08:37Z","content":"I will create the implementation plan for the **Cantor Dashboard Panels & UI Elements Audit**, structuring it element-by-element across every interactive control, metadata badge, document viewer, and layout split.","thinking":"**Auditing the Panel**\n\nI've shifted focus. The user corrected me, so I'm now concentrating on auditing the panel. I've set aside the information about matins and vespers, as it's not relevant. The cantor dashboard is the primary concern, so I'm diving back into that, and I'm putting the panel front and center.\n\n\n**Examining the UI**\n\nI'm now fully focused on the Cantor Dashboard UI. The user's input clarified the need for an element-by-element audit of the panels and controls. I've begun to examine the dashboard, specifically the top bar, liturgical date resolver, and control bar. I'm noting the logo, navigation tabs (Liturgical Calendar, Book Browser, Feast & Roadmap), theme toggle, and Recension badge, as well as the date picker and resolve control.\n\n\n**Analyzing the Elements**\n\nI'm now deep in the details of the Liturgical Parameter Overrides drawer, breaking down each control. I'm noting the recension source, Paschalion calendar system, and calendar source options, as well as the Temple Patronal Feast input and ceremonial rubrics. I'm also considering the Digest Layout Mode, developer tools toggle, and active parish profile management. Moving next to Panel 1.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":true,\"Summary\":\"Cantor Dashboard Panels and UI Elements Comprehensive Audit Plan.\",\"UserFacing\":true}","CodeContent":"\"<!-- [GENERATOR: Gemini 3.7 Flash] -->\\n# Implementation Plan — Cantor Dashboard Panels & UI Elements Audit\\n\\nThis plan establishes an element-by-element verification audit of all panels, controls, and data bindings in the **Cantor Dashboard** ([index.html](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/index.html), [main.js](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/main.js), and [style.css](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/style.css)) until `ALL ELEMENTS = PASS`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Dashboard Architecture & Panel Layout\\n\\nThe Cantor Dashboard is composed of 5 primary panel groups:\\n\\n```\\n┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\\n│                                 CANTOR DASHBOARD HEADER                                │\\n│ [Tab: Liturgical Calendar]  [Tab: Book Browser]  [Tab: Feast & Roadmap]  [Theme Toggle]│\\n├────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\\n│ LITURGICAL DATE RESOLVER BAR                                                           │\\n│ [Date Input] [Resolve Date] [Quick Jumps: Clean Monday | Thomas Sunday | Today | etc.] │\\n│ [▼ Liturgical Parameter Overrides Drawer]                                              │\\n├────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┬──────────────────\n<truncated 10141 bytes>","Description":"\"Create Cantor Dashboard Panels & UI Elements Audit Implementation Plan\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\augus\\\\/.gemini/antigravity/brain/68de5315-8f6d-40a7-84fc-f4db04ed3565/implementation_plan.md\"","toolAction":"\"Writing Cantor Dashboard audit plan\"","toolSummary":"\"Writing implementation_plan.md\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
